findings.body:
The setter guard was changed from `value <= 0` to `value < 0`, so `RetainedFileCountLimit = 0` no longer throws. `FileLoggerProvider.RollFiles` only deletes old files when `_maxRetainedFiles > 0`. A caller who sets 0 to mean "keep none" therefore gets unlimited retention and no error.

The error message still says "must be positive", and the new docs say the value is strictly positive or null. So the code now contradicts both its own message and its docs.

