The PR moves `validatableTypeInfo = null;` from the end of `TryGetValidatableTypeInfo` to the top. The result is the same: the loop overwrites the out value and the final null only matters on the false path. The change is harmless but unrelated to docs, and it adds diff noise.

::diff{file="src/Validation/src/ValidationOptions.cs" lines="44-56"}

Revert the move unless there is a reason to keep it. If it stays, mention it in the PR description.

The signature of `TryGetValidatableParameterInfo` now ends with ` {` on the same line, while the rest of the file (and the other method in this class) puts the brace on its own line. This is a whitespace-only change the doc PR does not need.

